#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/6
msgid ""
"Exactly the same. In fact, when you put on a\n"
"cardboard box when Snake In,\n"
msgstr ""
"完全一样。实际上，当Snake In穿上\n"
"纸箱时，\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/7
msgid ""
"both of you can climb inside.\n"
msgstr ""
"两人都能钻进去。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/8
msgid ""
"A box big enough to hold me and my buddy...\n"
msgstr ""
"能装下我和队友的大纸箱……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/9
msgid ""
"These are fine times we live in, eh, Kaz?\n"
msgstr ""
"真是个好时代啊，卡兹？\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/10
msgid ""
"Yyyyeah, sure, Boss...\n"
msgstr ""
"是……是啊，BOSS……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/0
msgid ""
"Snake, the R&D team came up with something new...\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，研发组搞出了新东西……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/1
msgid ""
"What is this?!\n"
msgstr ""
"这啥？！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/2
msgid ""
"It's a cardboard tank. It's got enough room for two\n"
"people,\n"
msgstr ""
"这是一辆纸板坦克。它足够容纳两\n"
"个人，\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/3
msgid ""
"same as any other cardboard box.\n"
msgstr ""
"跟普通纸箱一样。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/4
msgid ""
"Apparently the guy in front drives, and the guy in\n"
"back is the gunner...\n"
msgstr ""
"据说前面的人负责驾驶，后面的人\n"
"是炮手……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/5
msgid ""
"Hold on. Kaz, who the hell came up this thing?!\n"
msgstr ""
"等等。卡兹，谁搞出这玩意的？！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/6
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, Boss. He meant well, I swear.\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉，BOSS。他真是好意。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/7
msgid ""
"I know it's nowhere near as good as a real tank,\n"
"but still...\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道它远不如真正的坦克，\n"
"但还是……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/8
msgid ""
"It's BRILLIANT!!\n"
msgstr ""
"太棒了！！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/9
#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/10
#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/28
msgid ""
"Huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"啊？\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/10
msgid ""
"The perfect synthesis of stealth and attack power.\n"
msgstr ""
"隐匿与攻击力的完美结合。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/11
msgid ""
"Compact, elegant design. The finest example of a\n"
"weapon I've ever seen!\n"
msgstr ""
"紧凑、优雅的设计。这是我见过\n"
"最精良的武器典范！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/12
msgid ""
"Seriously, Kaz, I need to meet the guy who made\n"
"this. I wanna shake his hand.\n"
msgstr ""
"说真的，Kaz，我得见见做这个的\n"
"人。我想跟他握个手。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/13
msgid ""
"Y-you're serious? Snake, look at it, it's...\n"
msgstr ""
"你、当真？SNAKE，看它，这……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/14
msgid ""
"It's a masterpiece, in every sense of the word. You\n"
"don't agree?\n"
msgstr ""
"无论从哪方面说，这都是杰作。你\n"
"不同意？\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/15
msgid ""
"N-no, I...!\n"
msgstr ""
"不、不是，我……！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/16
msgid ""
"Ooh, what's that? A tank? I like it!\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，那是什么？坦克？我喜欢！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/17
msgid ""
"Paz?!\n"
msgstr ""
"帕兹？！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/18
msgid ""
"I hate tanks, but this one I think I could get used\n"
"to.\n"
msgstr ""
"我讨厌坦克，但这辆我能慢慢\n"
"习惯。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/19
msgid ""
"I love that it's a zero emissions vehicle - it will not\n"
"hurt the forests of Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"我喜欢它是零排放车辆——不会\n"
"伤害哥斯达黎加的森林。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/20
#: codec/2/912/0x3904c0/1
msgid ""
"What?!\n"
msgstr ""
"什么？！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/21
msgid ""
"Nice work, Kaz. I see I made the right choice\n"
"making you second in command.\n"
msgstr ""
"干得好，卡兹。看来我选你当\n"
"副手没选错。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/22
msgid ""
"But I... Is there something wrong with me?!\n"
msgstr ""
"可是我……我有什么问题吗？！\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/0
msgid ""
"Snake, about that cassette player Gálvez was\n"
"carrying...\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，加尔维斯带的那个\n"
"磁带播放器……\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/1
msgid ""
"What about it?\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么了？\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/2
msgid ""
"That was no Russian imitation.\n"
msgstr ""
"那不是苏联仿制品。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/3
msgid ""
"It was the real deal - a prototype developed by a\n"
"Japanese company.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是真货——一家日本公司\n"
"开发的试制品。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/4
msgid ""
"Get out of here!\n"
msgstr ""
"别逗了！\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/5
msgid ""
"It's true. It had the Sony logo on it. The product\n"
"name is \"WALKMAN.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。上面有索尼的标志。产品名\n"
"叫“WALKMAN”。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/6
msgid ""
"WALKMAN...\n"
msgstr ""
"WALKMAN……\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/7
msgid ""
"It's a revolutionary new concept. Music you can\n"
"listen to on the go.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是革命性的新概念。随时随地\n"
"听音乐。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/8
msgid ""
"You can take with you when you leave the house.\n"
msgstr ""
"出门也能带着走。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/9
msgid ""
"I gave it a listen,\n"
msgstr ""
"我听了听，\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/10
msgid ""
"and you wouldn't believe how good the sound\n"
"quality is for something so tiny.\n"
msgstr ""
"这么小的东西，音质好得\n"
"难以置信。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/11
msgid ""
"And in stereo, too. Think of the technology that\n"
"must have gone into it.\n"
msgstr ""
"还是立体声。想想得用上\n"
"多少技术。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/12
msgid ""
"And that tape is equally amazing.\n"
msgstr ""
"那磁带也一样惊人。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/13
msgid ""
"The treble range is clearly superior to any other\n"
"cassette ever made. Stylish, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"高音明显胜过以往任何磁带。\n"
"还很时髦。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/14
msgid ""
"How'd Gálvez get his hands on a model that's not\n"
"even out yet?\n"
msgstr ""
"加尔维斯怎么弄到还没上市的\n"
"型号的？\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/15
msgid ""
"Beats me. It's not the kind of thing I'd expect some\n"
"stodgy Soviet to be into.\n"
msgstr ""
"不知道。这不像古板苏联人\n"
"会喜欢的东西。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/16
msgid ""
"Me neither. Tell you what, though, it's a fine piece\n"
"of work.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也一样。不过说真的，这活儿\n"
"干得漂亮。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/17
msgid ""
"It'd let me listen to my music when I want, where I\n"
"want.\n"
msgstr ""
"这样我就能随时听音乐，\n"
"想听就听。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/18
msgid ""
"I... never thought I'd hear you say that. But I have\n"
"to agree.\n"
msgstr ""
"我……没想过你会这么说。但我\n"
"得承认。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/19
msgid ""
"Me, I'm a recording freak,\n"
msgstr ""
"我可是个录音狂，\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/20
msgid ""
"and I always used to laugh at the idea of a\n"
"portable player.\n"
msgstr ""
"我以前总是嘲笑便携播放器\n"
"这种想法。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/21
msgid ""
"But now that I've seen it in action, I've changed my\n"
"mind.\n"
msgstr ""
"但亲眼见它实际效果后，我\n"
"改主意了。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/22
msgid ""
"Being able to take your music with you...\n"
msgstr ""
"能把音乐随身带着……\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/23
msgid ""
"This could be the start of a revolution in music.\n"
msgstr ""
"这可能是音乐革命的开始。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/24
msgid ""
"Could be.\n"
msgstr ""
"有可能。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/25
msgid ""
"I'm having the guys at Mother Base study and\n"
"analyze it. Who knows?\n"
msgstr ""
"我让母基地的人研究\n"
"分析它。谁知道呢？\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/26
msgid ""
"They might be able to come up with something\n"
"even better.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们也许能做出\n"
"更好的东西。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 445..1421
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/0
msgid ""
"Going by this map, you've got a lot of different\n"
"terrain types between\n"
msgstr ""
"看这地图，从你到关押桑地诺\n"
"指挥官的小屋之间\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 1421..2396
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/1
msgid ""
"you and the hut where the Sandinista\n"
"comandante's being held.\n"
msgstr ""
"要经过许多不同的\n"
"地形类型。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 2674..3566
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/2
msgid ""
"Looks that way, doesn't it. Starting with jungle.\n"
msgstr ""
"看起来是这样。先是丛林。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 3580..4304
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/3
msgid ""
"The enemy won't be able to see you very well,\n"
msgstr ""
"敌人不容易看到你，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 4318..5433
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/4
msgid ""
"but your visibility won't be so hot, either. Stay alert.\n"
msgstr ""
"但你的视野也不怎么样。保持警惕。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 5489..6213
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/5
msgid ""
"Next you've got the swamps along the river.\n"
msgstr ""
"接下来是河边的沼泽。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 6255..7537
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/6
msgid ""
"Make sure you get a good feel for how robust\n"
"surveillance is before diving in.\n"
msgstr ""
"潜入之前，务必摸清\n"
"监视的严密程度。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 7565..7857
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 12329..12636
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/7
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/12
msgid ""
"Will do.\n"
msgstr ""
"好。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 7941..9292
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/8
msgid ""
"Finally, there's the boat repair cabin - the\n"
"comandante's in there.\n"
msgstr ""
"最后是修船小屋——\n"
"指挥官就在那里。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 9362..10421
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/9
msgid ""
"It's a key enemy outpost, and security is going to\n"
"be tight.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是敌人的重要前哨，安保会\n"
"非常严密。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 10448..11270
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/10
msgid ""
"You may have to let brute force do the talking.\n"
msgstr ""
"可能得靠硬闯了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 11312..11897
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/11
msgid ""
"You still have a long way to go, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"你还有很长的路要走，SNAKE。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 11911..12928
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/12
msgid ""
"Use caution, and don't make a racket out there.\n"
"Got it?\n"
msgstr ""
"小心，别弄出太大动静。\n"
"明白吗？\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/0
msgid ""
"To get to your next objective,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/1
msgid ""
"you'll need to backtrack along the way you came\n"
"for a bit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 445..1852
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/0
msgid ""
"To destroy the barricade north of the village, you'll\n"
"need Composition 4 explosive.\n"
msgstr ""
"要炸毁村庄北面的路障，你需要\n"
"C4炸药。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 1866..2549
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/1
msgid ""
"You've handled C4 before, right, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"你以前用过C4吧，SNAKE？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 2563..3970
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/2
msgid ""
"Yeah. I've been a regular user since the days of C3.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，从C3那会儿我就一直用它。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 3970..4750
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/3
msgid ""
"C3... oh yeah, I remember.\n"
msgstr ""
"C3…对，我记得。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 4750..5865
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/4
msgid ""
"That stuff got brittle and useless in cold\n"
"temperatures, so they upgraded.\n"
msgstr ""
"那种东西在低温下会变脆失效，\n"
"所以他们升级了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 5893..6659
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/5
msgid ""
"C4's a moldable plastic explosive.\n"
msgstr ""
"C4是可塑炸药。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 6673..7634
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/6
msgid ""
"It's very stable and won't explode without a special\n"
"detonator.\n"
msgstr ""
"它非常稳定，没有专用雷管\n"
"是不会爆炸的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 7662..8414
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/7
msgid ""
"Light it on fire and all it does is burn.\n"
msgstr ""
"用火点它只会燃烧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 8428..9418
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/8
msgid ""
"A lot of American soldiers in Vietnam used to use\n"
"it as fuel.\n"
msgstr ""
"越战时很多美军士兵\n"
"拿它当燃料用。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 9445..10504
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/9
msgid ""
"Place it near the barricade and move to a safe\n"
"location,\n"
msgstr ""
"放路障附近，然后转移到\n"
"安全位置，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 10532..11215
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/10
msgid ""
"then hit the detonator button to blow it up\n"
msgstr ""
"再按起爆按钮炸掉它\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 11215..11563
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/11
msgid ""
"I'm on it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我来。\n"

#: codec/1/172/0xac930/0
msgid ""
"We've completed work on the C4 charges. Equip\n"
"them at the entry gate and take them with you on\n"
"the mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"C4炸药我们已经完成了。在入口大门处\n"
"装备好，执行任务时\n"
"随身带上。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 515..1685
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/0
msgid ""
"Those giant footprints near the terminal... What do\n"
"you think they were, Kaz?\n"
msgstr ""
"终端附近那些巨大的脚印……你觉得\n"
"那是什么，Kaz？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 1699..2814
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/1
msgid ""
"It beats me... They're way too big, even for an\n"
"elephant.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也搞不懂……那太大了，就算是\n"
"大象也没那么大。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 2869..3887
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/2
msgid ""
"Made me think of that basilisco Chico was talking\n"
"about.\n"
msgstr ""
"让我想起了Chico说的\n"
"那种蛇怪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 4096..4513
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/3
msgid ""
"Hope it's not for real...\n"
msgstr ""
"希望不是真的……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 4527..5530
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/4
msgid ""
"Same here. If they really do have that kind of\n"
"weapon...\n"
msgstr ""
"我也是。如果它们真有那种\n"
"武器……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 5544..6492
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/5
msgid ""
"we could be dealing with a basilisk in more than\n"
"just looks.\n"
msgstr ""
"那我们面对的蛇怪可能不只是\n"
"外表像而已。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 6492..6729
#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 1434..1685
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 3691..4012
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/6
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/1
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/2
#: codec/2/915/0x393270/15
msgid ""
"What do you mean?\n"
msgstr ""
"什么意思？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 6729..8038
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/7
msgid ""
"There's a medieval encyclopedia that describes the\n"
"basilisk like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"有一本中世纪百科全书是这样描述\n"
"蛇怪的：\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 8066..9835
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/8
msgid ""
"\"The basilisk is the king of snakes. All snakes fear\n"
"the basilisk and flee at its sight...\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“蛇怪是蛇中之王。所有蛇都惧怕\n"
"蛇怪，一见它就逃……”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 9849..10546
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/9
msgid ""
"\"Lest they be slain by its foul breath.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“以免被它的毒气杀死。”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 10546..11243
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/10
msgid ""
"A snake to take out a snake, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"以蛇制蛇，是吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 11270..12315
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/11
msgid ""
"I don't mean to scare you or anything... but it never\n"
"hurts to be careful.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不是想吓你什么的……但小心\n"
"总没坏处。\n"

#: codec/1/172/0xaced0/0
msgid ""
"Apparently each part of an AI weapon is\n"
"connected to a memory board inside the AI pod.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/172/0xaced0/1
msgid ""
"Destroying a part will release the lock on the\n"
"memory board.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/172/0xaced0/2
msgid ""
"After that, climb in the pod and you'll be able to\n"
"grab whichever boards you've unlocked.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/0
msgid ""
"Damn, that base is even more heavily guarded than\n"
"Amanda's men said it would be...\n"
msgstr ""
"该死，那个基地的守卫比\n"
"Amanda的人说的还要森严……\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/1
msgid ""
"No kidding. It's gonna be tough to crack without\n"
"some serious hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"可不是嘛。没有点重装备\n"
"可不好攻进去。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/2
msgid ""
"You may end up having to fight fire with fire, so be\n"
"ready to use force if necessary.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可能不得不以牙还牙，所以必要时要做好\n"
"使用武力的准备。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/3
msgid ""
"Take as many weapons and items as you can\n"
"carry.\n"
msgstr ""
"尽量多带武器和\n"
"物品。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/4
msgid ""
"The more protection you have, the better.\n"
msgstr ""
"防护越多越好。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/5
msgid ""
"Roger. I'll keep that in mind when I pick my suit.\n"
msgstr ""
"收到，选衣服时我会记住。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/6
msgid ""
"I'll meet up with you ASAP, Snake. Hang tight for\n"
"just a little longer.\n"
msgstr ""
"我会尽快和你碰头，Snake。再坚持\n"
"一小会儿。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/7
#: codec/2/918/0x396100/10
msgid ""
"You got it.\n"
msgstr ""
"明白。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/0
msgid ""
"Right now there don't appear to be any enemy\n"
"soldiers in the area.\n"
msgstr ""
"目前该区域似乎没有任何敌方\n"
"士兵。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/1
msgid ""
"Relax and concentrate on your target practice.\n"
msgstr ""
"放松，专心打靶。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/2
msgid ""
"And don't forget to look for targets in the shadows\n"
"near the crates and forklifts.\n"
msgstr ""
"别忘了在板条箱和叉车附近的阴影中\n"
"寻找目标。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/3
msgid ""
"These are medium-range targets.\n"
msgstr ""
"这些是中距离目标。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/4
msgid ""
"You may want to consider taking something like an\n"
"assault rifle with you.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可以考虑带上类似突击步枪的\n"
"武器。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/5
msgid ""
"But I'll leave that up to you. Use whatever weapon\n"
"you want to get some practice.\n"
msgstr ""
"但这由你决定。用你想用的任何武器\n"
"来练练手吧。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/0
msgid ""
"We've already taken care of the enemy soldiers in\n"
"there.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们已经解决了那里的敌方\n"
"士兵。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/1
msgid ""
"It should be deserted.\n"
msgstr ""
"应该空无一人。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/2
msgid ""
"All you need to do is focus on hitting those targets.\n"
msgstr ""
"你只管专心打中那些目标。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/3
msgid ""
"It's geared toward long-range target practice.\n"
msgstr ""
"这里适合远距离打靶。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/4
msgid ""
"You should think about bringing something like a\n"
"sniper rifle.\n"
msgstr ""
"你应该考虑带上类似狙击步枪的\n"
"武器。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/5
msgid ""
"Then again, nothing's stopping you from giving it a\n"
"shot with a handgun, either.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过话说回来，用手枪试一试也\n"
"没什么不可以。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/0
msgid ""
"We've cleared this prison out already.\n"
msgstr ""
"这座监狱我们已经清空了。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/1
msgid ""
"No enemies to worry about in there.\n"
msgstr ""
"里面没有敌人。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/2
msgid ""
"I'm thinking you could use these twisty streets for\n"
"urban combat training.\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得你可以利用这些蜿蜒的街道进行\n"
"城市战斗训练。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/3
msgid ""
"This could be the perfect place to practice with\n"
"throwing weapons.\n"
msgstr ""
"这可能是练习投掷武器的完美\n"
"地点。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/4
msgid ""
"What do you think?\n"
msgstr ""
"你觉得呢？\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/0
msgid ""
"No sign of the enemy in there. You should be clear\n"
"to focus on training.\n"
msgstr ""
"那里没有敌人的迹象。你应该可以放心\n"
"专注于训练。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/1
msgid ""
"Some of the targets might be a little hard to spot,\n"
msgstr ""
"有些目标可能不太好找，\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/2
msgid ""
"but keep at it - they're out there somewhere.\n"
msgstr ""
"但别停，他们肯定在某个地方。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/3
msgid ""
"This is a medium-range area.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是中距离区域。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/4
msgid ""
"Good for whatever weapon you want to practice\n"
"with.\n"
msgstr ""
"练哪种武器都合适。\n"
"用它来练吧。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/5
msgid ""
"Aim quick, and aim true.\n"
msgstr ""
"瞄准要快，要准。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xaddb0/0
msgid ""
"The enemy presence in these barracks has been\n"
"neutralized.\n"
msgstr ""
"这些兵营里的敌人已被\n"
"清除。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xaddb0/1
msgid ""
"It's all yours now for target practice.\n"
msgstr ""
"现在归你打靶用了。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xaddb0/2
msgid ""
"The key to hitting all the targets within the time\n"
"limit\n"
msgstr ""
"在时限内命中所有目标的关键\n"
"所在\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xaddb0/3
msgid ""
"is cutting down on movement time.\n"
msgstr ""
"是减少移动时间。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xaddb0/4
msgid ""
"Some of them you may find easiest to hit from a\n"
"sniping position up on the roof.\n"
msgstr ""
"其中一些目标，从屋顶上的\n"
"狙击位置最容易命中。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xaddb0/5
msgid ""
"Not that it wouldn't be an effective way to train\n"
"with other weapons, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"这并不是说它不能有效地用来\n"
"训练其他武器。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae030/0
msgid ""
"As you're probably aware, this is a Fulton recovery\n"
"mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"你大概知道，这是一次富尔顿回收\n"
"任务。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae030/1
msgid ""
"Be careful you don't shoot and kill any prisoners by\n"
"accident.\n"
msgstr ""
"小心不要误射\n"
"杀死任何俘虏。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae030/2
msgid ""
"And don't forget to take the recovery kit with you.\n"
msgstr ""
"别忘了带上回收装备。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae030/3
msgid ""
"I'd suggest arming yourself with a tranquilizer gun\n"
"just to be safe\n"
msgstr ""
"为安全起见，我建议你装备\n"
"麻醉枪\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae030/4
msgid ""
"- so you don't kill any prisoners.\n"
msgstr ""
"- 免得打死俘虏。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae250/0
msgid ""
"This is a sweep-and-destroy mission, not a\n"
"sneaking mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是扫荡歼灭任务，不是\n"
"潜行任务。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae250/1
msgid ""
"Don't think you're going to slip through this one\n"
"unnoticed. You will fight.\n"
msgstr ""
"别以为你能悄无声息地\n"
"溜过去。你得战斗。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae250/2
msgid ""
"Forget about your camo index.\n"
msgstr ""
"别管迷彩指数了。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae250/3
msgid ""
"What's more important is choosing gear that offers\n"
"physical protection.\n"
msgstr ""
"更重要的是选择能提供\n"
"物理防护的装备。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae250/4
msgid ""
"And of course you'll need a big enough arsenal to\n"
"take care of business.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，你还需要足够多的武器\n"
"来完成任务。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae250/5
msgid ""
"Oh, and don't forget your recovery items, either!\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，也别忘了带恢复道具！\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/0
msgid ""
"To hold up an enemy, you need to get behind them\n"
"without being seen.\n"
msgstr ""
"要挟持敌人，得先不被发现\n"
"绕到其身后。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/1
msgid ""
"Get close enough without their noticing, point your\n"
"weapon,\n"
msgstr ""
"在不被察觉的情况下靠近，用枪\n"
"指向他们，\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/2
msgid ""
"and even a trained soldier will reach for the sky.\n"
msgstr ""
"再训练有素的士兵也会举手投降。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/3
msgid ""
"No sense in holding up an enemy only to have his\n"
"buddies attack you, though.\n"
msgstr ""
"但挟持敌人却招来同伴\n"
"攻击你，就没意义了。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/4
msgid ""
"Make sure you get them when they're alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"趁他们落单时动手。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/5
msgid ""
"And be careful you don't shoot them by mistake.\n"
msgstr ""
"小心别误射他们。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/6
msgid ""
"Kill a soldier here and you fail the mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"在此杀士兵会导致任务失败。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae7b0/0
msgid ""
"A real veteran ought to be able to take out\n"
"multiple enemies with a single bullet.\n"
msgstr ""
"真正的老兵应该能用一发子弹\n"
"干掉多个敌人。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae7b0/1
msgid ""
"Not by shooting them, but by using it to set off an\n"
"explosion.\n"
msgstr ""
"不是直接射人，而是用它引发\n"
"爆炸。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae7b0/2
msgid ""
"Find something flammable,\n"
msgstr ""
"找些易燃物，\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae7b0/3
msgid ""
"like a gasoline drum or an unmanned weapon with\n"
"a full fuel tank...\n"
msgstr ""
"比如汽油桶或油箱满载的\n"
"无人兵器……\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae7b0/4
msgid ""
"Then shoot it and blow it up. And make sure it\n"
"takes a few enemies with it!\n"
msgstr ""
"然后射击引爆。务必让它\n"
"连带干掉几个敌人！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 459..1504
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/0
msgid ""
"This is a sniping mission. So don't forget your\n"
"sniper rifle.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是狙击任务。别忘了带\n"
"狙击步枪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 1574..2702
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/1
msgid ""
"When equipping a sniper rifle, you can look through\n"
"the scope to aim.\n"
msgstr ""
"装备狙击步枪后，可以通过\n"
"瞄准镜瞄准。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 2786..4082
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/2
msgid ""
"You can change the scope's zoom level by\n"
"pressing <I=ZOOMIN> and <I=ZOOMOUT>.\n"
msgstr ""
"按<I=ZOOMIN>和<I=ZOOMOUT>\n"
"可调整瞄准镜倍率。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 4179..5335
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/3
msgid ""
"Keep in mind, though, that using the scope cuts\n"
"down your field of vision.\n"
msgstr ""
"但记住，使用瞄准镜会\n"
"缩小视野。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 5363..6673
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/4
msgid ""
"You'll want to be pointing in the right general\n"
"direction before taking aim.\n"
msgstr ""
"瞄准前先大致对准\n"
"正确方向。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 6743..7230
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/5
msgid ""
"When aiming at distant targets,\n"
msgstr ""
"瞄准远处目标时，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 7286..8205
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/6
msgid ""
"even a slight hand tremor can throw your aim way\n"
"off.\n"
msgstr ""
"哪怕手轻微抖动也会让准头\n"
"偏得离谱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 8275..8916
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/7
msgid ""
"Just stay still and compose yourself,\n"
msgstr ""
"保持静止，稳住自己，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 8986..10058
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/8
msgid ""
"and before long the tremors should calm down\n"
"naturally.\n"
msgstr ""
"过一会儿抖动就会\n"
"自然平息。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 10142..11257
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/9
msgid ""
"Keeping low to the ground will also help you\n"
"maintain your aim.\n"
msgstr ""
"压低身体贴地也有助于\n"
"保持瞄准。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 11354..11674
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/10
msgid ""
"You got all that?\n"
msgstr ""
"记住了？\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/0
msgid ""
"In this mission, you're prohibited from killing any\n"
"enemy combatants.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/1
msgid ""
"And if you're spotted even once, you fail.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/2
msgid ""
"Bottom line: proceed with caution.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/3
msgid ""
"Stay low to the ground. If there are any enemies\n"
"nearby,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/4
msgid ""
"walk slowly and don't make a sound…\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/5
msgid ""
"Another good technique is to hide behind\n"
"something\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/6
msgid ""
"and do <I=ESEARCH> to check out your enemies.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/7
msgid ""
"And then there's always the classic trick of\n"
"throwing\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 459..1546
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/0
msgid ""
"So all I have to do here is shoot down the Fulton\n"
"recovery balloons, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以我只要射下富尔顿\n"
"回收气球就行了吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 1560..2716
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/1
msgid ""
"Right. And don't shoot the soldier dangling\n"
"underneath by mistake.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。别误射下面\n"
"吊着的士兵。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 2744..3204
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/2
msgid ""
"I'd go with the sniper rifle,\n"
msgstr ""
"我会选狙击步枪，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 3204..4193
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/3
msgid ""
"but really, any weapon will work as long as you aim\n"
"carefully.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过只要仔细瞄准，\n"
"什么武器都行。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 4472..5001
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/4
msgid ""
"Balloon popping... heh.\n"
msgstr ""
"打气球……嘿。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 5001..5907
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/5
msgid ""
"You might get more balloons if you do this one as\n"
"a CO-OPS.\n"
msgstr ""
"用合作任务打这关\n"
"气球可能更多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 5907..6784
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/6
msgid ""
"The, uh... ha, ha... sky's the limit!\n"
msgstr ""
"那啥…哈哈…上不封顶！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 6812..7202
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/7
msgid ""
"Look at it this way\n"
msgstr ""
"这么想吧\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 7202..8512
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/8
msgid ""
"- it'd get real depressing real quick if every single\n"
"mission were a bloodbath.\n"
msgstr ""
"——要是每个任务都血流成河，\n"
"人很快就崩溃了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 8596..9766
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/9
msgid ""
"It's good to have a nice, relaxing challenge like this\n"
"once in a while, you know?\n"
msgstr ""
"偶尔来点轻松点的挑战\n"
"也挺好，对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 9780..11340
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/10
msgid ""
"And c'mon, don't those Fulton balloons look tasty?\n"
"Like big, juicy, floating pigs...\n"
msgstr ""
"再说，富尔顿气球不诱人吗？\n"
"像又大又多汁的飞天猪…\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 11368..12789
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/11
msgid ""
"...Yeah, sure, whatever. So this is called a \"Pooyan\n"
"mission.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"…行行行，随你。这就叫“Pooyan\n"
"任务”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 12831..13332
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/12
msgid ""
"What's that supposed to mean?\n"
msgstr ""
"那是什么意思？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 13360..14433
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/13
msgid ""
"When I was a kid, my neighbors had a pet pig they\n"
"called Pooyan.\n"
msgstr ""
"小时候邻居养了头宠物猪，\n"
"就叫Pooyan。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 14447..15617
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/14
msgid ""
"Every time I see a Fulton balloon, it reminds me of\n"
"that litle porker.\n"
msgstr ""
"每次看到富尔顿气球，我就想起\n"
"那头小猪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 15645..16913
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/15
msgid ""
"OK, but the objective here is to pop those\n"
"balloons, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"OK，但这里的目标是打爆那些\n"
"气球，对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 16983..18000
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/16
msgid ""
"Doesn't sound like a good idea getting emotionally\n"
"attached...\n"
msgstr ""
"听起来不太妙，投入感情会\n"
"陷进去的……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 18014..19365
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/17
msgid ""
"Good point. Man, if only those were real pigs\n"
"dangling from the balloons...\n"
msgstr ""
"有道理。唉，要是气球上吊的\n"
"是真猪就好了…\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 19379..19853
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/18
msgid ""
"Now wouldn't that be something...\n"
msgstr ""
"那可就厉害了…\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/0
msgid ""
"Enemies that steal your items will try and escape\n"
"the area.\n"
msgstr ""
"偷你道具的敌人会试图逃离\n"
"该区域。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/1
msgid ""
"Make it a priority to take them out first.\n"
msgstr ""
"优先干掉他们。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/2
msgid ""
"Don't let them make off with your stuff.\n"
msgstr ""
"别让他们带着你的东西跑了。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/3
msgid ""
"We're seeing multiple hostiles in this area.\n"
msgstr ""
"该区域发现多名敌人。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/4
msgid ""
"It's not going to be easy going it alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"单打独斗可不容易。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/5
msgid ""
"I'd recommend taking this one on as a two-man cell\n"
"in CO-OPS.\n"
msgstr ""
"建议在合作任务里\n"
"两人一组来打。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafb40/0
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you could try planting Claymores\n"
"along the routes they walk.\n"
msgstr ""
"或者，可以在他们的巡逻路线上\n"
"埋阔剑地雷。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafb40/1
msgid ""
"We need you to stop that nuke, Boss.\n"
msgstr ""
"BOSS，得阻止那枚核弹。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafb40/2
msgid ""
"We'll keep you safe, no matter what it takes!\n"
msgstr ""
"我们拼了命也会保护你！\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/0
msgid ""
"It's going to take more than small arms fire to take\n"
"down a truck.\n"
msgstr ""
"光靠轻武器打不掉\n"
"卡车。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/1
msgid ""
"Some kind of rocket's your best bet.\n"
msgstr ""
"最好用火箭筒。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/2
msgid ""
"Another tactic to try would be setting off an\n"
"explosion from afar.\n"
msgstr ""
"也可以试试从远处\n"
"引爆。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/3
msgid ""
"You could also call in a support strike,\n"
msgstr ""
"还可以呼叫支援打击，\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/4
msgid ""
"if you can manage to tag them with a marker...\n"
msgstr ""
"只要能先用标记器标上他们……\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafea0/0
msgid ""
"It'll take more than one missile to sink Mother\n"
"Base, but if we do get hit,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xafea0/1
msgid ""
"we'll obviously need time, manpower, and materials\n"
"to repair the damage.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xafea0/2
msgid ""
"Do everything you can to keep Mother Base safe.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xafea0/3
msgid ""
"And, ah, at the risk of stating the obvious: if a\n"
"missile hits you,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/176/0xb00d0/0
msgid ""
"You'll be using C4 for demolition.\n"
msgstr ""
"爆破要用C4。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb00d0/1
msgid ""
"As you might imagine, it's gonna make a big noise\n"
"when it detonates.\n"
msgstr ""
"可以想象，引爆的时候\n"
"会发出巨大的声响。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb00d0/2
msgid ""
"For your own safety, make sure you put plenty of\n"
"distance\n"
msgstr ""
"为了自身安全，务必\n"
"保持足够距离。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb00d0/3
msgid ""
"between yourself and the C4 before detonating it.\n"
msgstr ""
"离C4远一点。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb0290/0
msgid ""
"Boss, we're not sure where your gear is being\n"
"stored.\n"
msgstr ""
"老大，我们不知你的装备\n"
"存哪。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb0350/0
msgid ""
"Amanda and her crew tell me they've managed to\n"
"identify several different categories\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达的人告诉我，他们已成功\n"
"识别出几个不同类别。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb0350/1
msgid ""
"of mercenaries employed by the CIA.\n"
msgstr ""
"几类雇佣兵。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb0350/2
msgid ""
"Give me a rundown. Sounds like info I could use.\n"
msgstr ""
"说说看。听起来有用。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb0350/3
msgid ""
"No problem. I'll go through them in order.\n"
msgstr ""
"没问题，我按顺序讲。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 445..1058
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/0
msgid ""
"The type of enemy you'll be seeing most\n"
msgstr ""
"最常见的敌人类型，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 1058..2368
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/1
msgid ""
"is the type that patrols and guards a specific\n"
"operational area.\n"
msgstr ""
"是负责巡逻和守卫特定\n"
"作战区域的类型。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 2396..3775
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/2
msgid ""
"For the sake of convenience, Amanda's crew calls\n"
"the outdoor ones \"patrolmen,\"\n"
msgstr ""
"为方便起见，阿曼达的人把\n"
"室外的称为“巡逻兵”，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 3775..4374
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/3
msgid ""
"and the indoor ones \"guards.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"室内的叫“守卫”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 4388..5043
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/4
msgid ""
"They might look like they're just out for a stroll,\n"
msgstr ""
"他们看似只是在闲逛，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 5043..5907
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/5
msgid ""
"but don't be fooled - they're sharper than they\n"
"look.\n"
msgstr ""
"但别被骗了，他们比看起来\n"
"敏锐得多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 5948..6757
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/6
msgid ""
"All of their senses are finely honed.\n"
msgstr ""
"五感都极为灵敏。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 6812..7592
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/7
msgid ""
"Normally they'll patrol along fixed routes,\n"
msgstr ""
"通常沿固定路线巡逻，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 7592..8818
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/8
msgid ""
"but when the alert level is raised they'll assume a\n"
"more efficient alert posture\n"
msgstr ""
"但当警戒等级提升时，他们会采取\n"
"更高效的警戒姿态，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 8818..10156
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/9
msgid ""
"and focus on defending specific points. That's bad\n"
"for you.\n"
msgstr ""
"并专注于防守特定点位。这对你\n"
"很不利。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 10253..10978
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/10
msgid ""
"Obviously they can hold their own in combat,\n"
msgstr ""
"他们战斗力自然不弱，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 10978..12051
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/11
msgid ""
"and with body armor it'll be even harder to take\n"
"them down.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且有了防弹衣，就更难\n"
"干掉他们了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 12106..12692
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/12
msgid ""
"If they're wearing a bulletproof helmet,\n"
msgstr ""
"要是戴着防弹头盔，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 12705..13876
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/13
msgid ""
"you can forget about one-shot kills. Just a heads\n"
"up.\n"
msgstr ""
"别想一枪毙命了。就\n"
"提醒你下。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 13945..15116
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/14
msgid ""
"You'll need to be smart about using camo and pick\n"
"your routes.\n"
msgstr ""
"你必须善用迷彩，并谨慎选择\n"
"行进路线。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 15144..16063
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/15
msgid ""
"The most important thing is to avoid detection.\n"
msgstr ""
"最重要的是别被发现。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 445..1852
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/0
msgid ""
"When the enemy spots you and goes on alert, they\n"
"may call in a backup strike team.\n"
msgstr ""
"敌人发现你并警戒时，他们\n"
"可能呼叫后备突击队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 1866..3120
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/1
msgid ""
"These assault teams are heavily armed, well\n"
"trained, and highly dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""
"这些突击队装备精良、训练有素，\n"
"而且极其危险。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 3134..3873
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/2
msgid ""
"Amanda's crew calls them \"commandos.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达的人管他们叫“突击兵”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 3900..5670
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/3
msgid ""
"Unlike the patrolmen, these guys will actively,\n"
"relentlessly track and hunt you down - like hounds.\n"
msgstr ""
"与巡逻兵不同，这些家伙会主动、\n"
"无情地追踪猎杀你，像猎犬一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 6032..7216
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/4
msgid ""
"Hounds to hunt a former FOXHOUND... Bring it on.\n"
msgstr ""
"猎犬来猎前FOXHOUND……放马过来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 7244..8080
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/5
msgid ""
"They won't give up easily even if they lose sight of\n"
"you.\n"
msgstr ""
"即使跟丢了你，他们也不会\n"
"轻易放弃。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 8080..9083
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/6
msgid ""
"They'll clear out any likely hiding places they come\n"
"across.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们会搜查沿途遇到的\n"
"任何可能藏身之处。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 9097..10267
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/7
msgid ""
"So don't get too comfy in one spot or you might\n"
"get caught again.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以别在一处待太舒服，否则可能\n"
"再次被抓。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 10281..11173
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/8
msgid ""
"Keep your eyes fixed on them and what they're\n"
"doing.\n"
msgstr ""
"时刻盯紧他们以及他们\n"
"在做什么。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 11229..12329
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/9
msgid ""
"Also, be aware that commando gear includes body\n"
"armor.\n"
msgstr ""
"另外注意，突击队装备包括\n"
"防弹衣。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 12329..13305
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/10
msgid ""
"So don't think you can deal with them by going in\n"
"guns blazing.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以别以为你可以靠\n"
"猛冲猛打来对付他们。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 13305..14405
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/11
msgid ""
"All I've got to do is find an exposed weak point\n"
"and...\n"
msgstr ""
"我只需找到暴露的弱点\n"
"然后……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 14405..14767
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/12
msgid ""
"Exactly.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/0
msgid ""
"There's one type of commando you really need to\n"
"watch out for,\n"
msgstr ""
"有一种突击队员你特别需要\n"
"小心，\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/1
msgid ""
"and that's the kind toting shotguns.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是拿霰弹枪的那种。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/2
msgid ""
"They can take a few hits and still keep charging\n"
"you.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们能挨几枪，却仍继续向你\n"
"冲来。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/3
msgid ""
"And believe me, you don't want them closing in\n"
"between those shotgun blasts.\n"
msgstr ""
"相信我，你绝不想让他们在霰弹枪射击间隙\n"
"逼近你。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/4
msgid ""
"When they start charging, you need to stop them\n"
"immediately.\n"
msgstr ""
"当他们开始冲锋时，你必须立刻\n"
"阻止他们。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/5
msgid ""
"Use something with serious stopping power.\n"
msgstr ""
"用制止力强的武器。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 459..1643
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/0
msgid ""
"We've also confirmed that some of the enemies\n"
"specialize in ambushes.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们还确认，有些敌人\n"
"专门擅长伏击。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 1657..2424
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/1
msgid ""
"Amanda's crew calls them \"scouts.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达的人管他们叫“侦察兵”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 2479..3510
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/2
msgid ""
"They'll blend themselves in with the terrain and the\n"
"vegetation.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们会把自己与地形和\n"
"植被融为一体。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 3538..4263
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/3
msgid ""
"Then, when they see you, they'll swoop in.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后一看到你，就扑上来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 4318..4876
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/4
msgid ""
"They fight pretty much like commandos\n"
msgstr ""
"他们打法跟特种兵差不多\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 4876..5670
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/5
msgid ""
"and will use clearing techniques to flush you out.\n"
msgstr ""
"会用清场战术把你逼出来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 5726..7049
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/6
msgid ""
"In addition to wielding normal weapons, the scouts\n"
"also carry wires.\n"
msgstr ""
"侦察兵除了普通武器，\n"
"还带着钢丝。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 7077..8178
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/7
msgid ""
"Hm... Sounds like these guys know their CQC.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……看来这帮人懂CQC。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 8192..9640
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/8
msgid ""
"Could be. We've been getting reports of CQC\n"
"attacks being blocked by wires.\n"
msgstr ""
"有可能。我们收到报告说\n"
"CQC攻击被钢丝挡住了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 9668..10031
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/9
msgid ""
"Stay alert.\n"
msgstr ""
"警惕。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/0
msgid ""
"Scouts are outfitted with camouflage to help them\n"
"hide.\n"
msgstr ""
"侦察兵配有迷彩，\n"
"方便隐蔽。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/1
msgid ""
"Some of them look kind of weird, like they've got\n"
"seaweed growing all over them.\n"
msgstr ""
"有些看着挺怪，\n"
"像长了一身海藻。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/2
msgid ""
"Ah, ghillie suits.\n"
msgstr ""
"啊，吉利服。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/3
msgid ""
"Not much difference between them and any other\n"
"scout in terms of combat ability,\n"
msgstr ""
"战斗力跟其他侦察兵\n"
"没多大差别，\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/4
msgid ""
"but it does make them harder to spot.\n"
msgstr ""
"但确实更难发现。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/5
msgid ""
"I'm sure it does.\n"
msgstr ""
"那肯定。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/6
msgid ""
"You've come across these before?\n"
msgstr ""
"你以前遇到过？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/7
msgid ""
"Yeah. The Soviet Union...\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯。苏联……\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/8
msgid ""
"The first time, it took me a full hour to find the\n"
"guy and take him out...\n"
msgstr ""
"第一次我花了整整一小时\n"
"才找到他干掉……\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/9
msgid ""
"Kaz, do you know if they shine?\n"
msgstr ""
"卡兹，他们会发光吗？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/10
msgid ""
"...Shine. Like how?\n"
msgstr ""
"……发光。怎么发？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/11
msgid ""
"Like from their heads.\n"
msgstr ""
"从头上。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/12
msgid ""
"Their heads?\n"
msgstr ""
"头上？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/13
msgid ""
"How about their hair? Do they have a lot of it?\n"
msgstr ""
"头发呢？多不多？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/14
msgid ""
"What are you talking about? How the hell would I\n"
"know?\n"
msgstr ""
"你在说什么？我他妈怎么\n"
"会知道？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/15
msgid ""
"How about a parrot? Did anybody hear a parrot\n"
"squawk?\n"
msgstr ""
"鹦鹉怎么样？有人听到鹦鹉\n"
"叫吗？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/16
msgid ""
"A parrot? Look, Snake, you're talking to the wrong\n"
"guy.\n"
msgstr ""
"鹦鹉？听着，Snake，你找错\n"
"人了。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/17
msgid ""
"I mean, Cecile's the bird expert...\n"
msgstr ""
"塞西尔才是鸟类专家……\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/18
msgid ""
"Wait a second, what am I saying? You're not\n"
"making any sense to begin with!\n"
msgstr ""
"等等，我在说什么？\n"
"你本来就说得没头没脑！\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/19
msgid ""
"Never mind. It's... a long story. I'll figure out another\n"
"way. Forget about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"算了。这事……说来话长。我再想别的\n"
"办法吧。别管了。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/20
msgid ""
"Yeah, I'll do that.\n"
msgstr ""
"好，就这么办。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/21
msgid ""
"Anyway, we've already lost too many good people\n"
"to these surprise encounters.\n"
msgstr ""
"总之，这些遭遇战已经让我们损失了太多\n"
"好手。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/22
msgid ""
"Make sure you don't end up like one of them.\n"
msgstr ""
"别让自己也变成其中之一。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 445..1128
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/0
msgid ""
"There are areas out there where enemy soldiers\n"
"are\n"
msgstr ""
"有些区域里，敌人士兵\n"
"会\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 1128..2048
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/1
msgid ""
"deployed in multiple layers for extra coverage.\n"
msgstr ""
"多层布防，覆盖更严密。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 2075..2995
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/2
msgid ""
"More than a few of those will be attacking you\n"
"from a distance\n"
msgstr ""
"其中不少人会从远处\n"
"向你发起攻击\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 60749..11426
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/3
msgid ""
"- rooftops and far-off vantage points.\n"
msgstr ""
"——屋顶和远处的制高点。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/4
msgid ""
"Try not to get too distracted by nearby enemies,\n"
msgstr ""
"别被近处的敌人分散太多注意，\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/5
msgid ""
"because you could be leaving yourself wide open\n"
"to longer-range attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"因为那样你会完全暴露在\n"
"更远距离的攻击下。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 7356..7787
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 5517..5921
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/6
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/8
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/5
msgid ""
"I'll be careful.\n"
msgstr ""
"我会小心。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 445..1030
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/0
msgid ""
"Enemy tanks, armored vehicles,\n"
msgstr ""
"敌方坦克、装甲车\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 1030..2173
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/1
msgid ""
"and attack choppers are always accompanied by a\n"
"combat squad.\n"
msgstr ""
"而攻击直升机身边总跟着一支\n"
"战斗小队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 2229..3051
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/2
msgid ""
"The soldiers aren't particularly tough on their own.\n"
msgstr ""
"那些士兵单打独斗并不算强。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 3078..4263
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/3
msgid ""
"What makes them formidable is how well they work\n"
"together as a team.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们难对付，就在于配合得\n"
"像一支队伍般默契。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 4291..5126
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/4
msgid ""
"As if you didn't have enough to worry about with\n"
"the machine.\n"
msgstr ""
"好像光应付那台机器还不够你\n"
"操心似的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 5140..5795
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/5
msgid ""
"Good. I like a challenge.\n"
msgstr ""
"好。我喜欢挑战。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 5809..7035
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/6
msgid ""
"Yeah, well, see how you feel when you actually\n"
"have to face them in battle.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，等你真在战斗中\n"
"面对它们，再看是什么感觉吧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 7091..8052
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/7
msgid ""
"Snake, whatever you do, don't let them surround\n"
"you.\n"
msgstr ""
"Snake，千万别让它们把你\n"
"包围了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 8066..9097
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/8
msgid ""
"The last thing you need is to get pushed into the\n"
"vehicle's kill zone.\n"
msgstr ""
"你最不想遇到的就是被逼进\n"
"载具的杀伤区。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 9153..10086
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/9
msgid ""
"And pay attention to what your enemies say to\n"
"each other.\n"
msgstr ""
"还要注意听敌人彼此之间\n"
"在说什么。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 10114..11201
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/10
msgid ""
"You can improve your chances by figuring out\n"
"what they're planning\n"
msgstr ""
"弄清他们\n"
"在谋划什么，能提高你的胜算\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 11215..11939
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/11
msgid ""
"and using it to preempt their movements.\n"
msgstr ""
"并借此抢先行动。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 11967..12845
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/12
msgid ""
"You don't always have to go toe to toe to win a\n"
"fight.\n"
msgstr ""
"要赢一场战斗，并不非得\n"
"正面硬拼。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 12873..13500
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/13
msgid ""
"Think like a guerrilla.\n"
msgstr ""
"像游击队员那样思考。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 459..1476
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/0
msgid ""
"Enemies carrying shields can be a real pain in the\n"
"ass.\n"
msgstr ""
"携带盾牌的敌人真是让人头疼得\n"
"要命。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 1532..2424
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/1
msgid ""
"To hear Amanda tell it, trying to fight those\n"
"bastards\n"
msgstr ""
"听阿曼达说，想跟那些\n"
"混蛋交手\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 2424..3371
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/2
msgid ""
"while they sit behind their shields taking pistol\n"
"shots at you\n"
msgstr ""
"他们却躲在盾牌后面朝你\n"
"开枪\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 3385..4109
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/3
msgid ""
"is enough to make you want to rip your hair out.\n"
msgstr ""
"能把你气得抓狂。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 4165..4778
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/4
msgid ""
"Get around and flank them if you can.\n"
msgstr ""
"能绕就绕到侧面包抄。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 4820..5976
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/5
msgid ""
"You might want to try blinding them with smoke or\n"
"stun grenades first.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可先用烟雾弹或\n"
"眩晕手雷让他们失明。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 6046..7509
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/6
msgid ""
"Also, armor-piercing rounds should make it a little\n"
"easier to punch through their shields.\n"
msgstr ""
"另外，穿甲弹应该能让你更容易\n"
"击穿他们的盾牌。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 7551..8066
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/7
msgid ""
"Use 'em if you've got 'em.\n"
msgstr ""
"有就用。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 459..1769
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/0
msgid ""
"We know there are variations in the kinds of gear\n"
"patrolmen and commandos wear,\n"
msgstr ""
"我们知道巡逻兵和突击队员穿戴的装备\n"
"种类存在差异，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 1769..2284
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/1
msgid ""
"especially the body armor.\n"
msgstr ""
"尤其是护甲。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 2326..3510
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/2
msgid ""
"Our scouts report that an enemy's defense and\n"
"firing accuracy\n"
msgstr ""
"侦察兵报告，敌人的防御和\n"
"射击精准度\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 3510..4472
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/3
msgid ""
"are directly proportional to how heavy their gear is.\n"
msgstr ""
"与装备重量成正比。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 4750..5628
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/4
msgid ""
"Those must be the guys with the highest combat\n"
"skills.\n"
msgstr ""
"那些人肯定就是战斗\n"
"技能最高的家伙。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 5656..6659
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/5
msgid ""
"They can fight in heavier gear without their\n"
"performance suffering.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们能穿着更重的装备作战，而\n"
"表现不会下降。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 6673..7857
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/6
msgid ""
"Supposedly it's pretty easy to tell the difference in\n"
"gear just by looking.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说光靠看就能很容易分辨出\n"
"装备的差异。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 7927..8233
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/7
msgid ""
"So remember:\n"
msgstr ""
"记住：\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 8233..9334
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/8
msgid ""
"use extra caution when dealing with enemies\n"
"wearing heavy gear.\n"
msgstr ""
"对付穿着重型装备的敌人时\n"
"要格外小心。\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2c50/0
msgid ""
"Enemies will try to fight you from different\n"
"distances\n"
msgstr ""
"敌人会尝试从不同的\n"
"距离与你交战\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2c50/1
msgid ""
"based on the weapon they've got equipped.\n"
msgstr ""
"在不同距离与你交战。\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2c50/2
msgid ""
"When you meet an enemy, get a good look at what\n"
"they're carrying\n"
msgstr ""
"遇到敌人时，仔细看清他们\n"
"拿着什么\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2c50/3
msgid ""
"- it can make or break your chances in battle.\n"
msgstr ""
"——这能决定战斗成败。\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2e10/0
msgid ""
"Enemies carrying handguns and shotguns will try\n"
"and get in close.\n"
msgstr ""
"携带手枪和霰弹枪的敌人会试图\n"
"靠近你。\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2e10/1
msgid ""
"That makes them dangerous, but at the same time\n"
"easier to hit.\n"
msgstr ""
"这让他们很危险，但同时也\n"
"更容易被击中。\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2e10/2
msgid ""
"Keep you wits about you and you can turn a threat\n"
"into an opportunity.\n"
msgstr ""
"保持头脑清醒，你就能把威胁\n"
"变成机会。\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/0
msgid ""
"Don't expect enemies carrying sniper rifles\n"
msgstr ""
"别指望拿狙击枪的敌人\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/1
msgid ""
"or rocket launchers to get up close and personal.\n"
msgstr ""
"或者用火箭筒近身招呼。\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/2
msgid ""
"They'll be constantly moving from place to place\n"
msgstr ""
"他们会不停转移位置\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/3
msgid ""
"looking for an opening to snipe at you. Tricky\n"
"bastards.\n"
msgstr ""
"找机会狙击你。狡猾的\n"
"家伙。\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/4
msgid ""
"Eye for an eye, tooth for a tooth, - go with the\n"
"sniper rifle.\n"
msgstr ""
"以眼还眼，以牙还牙，- 用\n"
"狙击步枪上。\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/5
msgid ""
"Make sure you stay out of their line of sight,\n"
msgstr ""
"务必别进入他们视线，\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/6
msgid ""
"and when they expose themselves, take 'em down!\n"
msgstr ""
"等他们露头，就干掉！\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb33f0/0
#: codec/1/179/0xb3490/0
#: codec/1/179/0xb3530/0
#: codec/1/179/0xb35d0/0
#: codec/1/179/0xb3670/0
msgid ""
"(dummy. not used)\n"
msgstr ""
"（占位）\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 473..1226
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica means \"rich coast\" in Spanish.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加在西班牙语里意为\"富饶海岸\"。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 1267..2089
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/1
msgid ""
"Is it true that Columbus was the one who came up\n"
"with the name?\n"
msgstr ""
"真是哥伦布起的\n"
"名字吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 2173..3092
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/2
msgid ""
"Your guess is as good as mine. But it is true\n"
msgstr ""
"我也说不准。但确实\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 3092..4388
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/3
msgid ""
"that Columbus landed his ships near Limón back in\n"
"the Age of Exploration.\n"
msgstr ""
"当年哥伦布在大航海时代\n"
"把他的船停靠在利蒙附近。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 4458..5154
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/4
msgid ""
"He wrote in his diary that when he landed,\n"
msgstr ""
"他在日记里写道，登陆时\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 5224..6352
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/5
msgid ""
"the indígena showered him with gifts of gold.\n"
"Hence the name.\n"
msgstr ""
"原住民献给他大量黄金作礼。\n"
"因此得名。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 6394..6938
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/6
msgid ""
"It sounds a little strange to me.\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得有点奇怪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 7007..7955
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/7
msgid ""
"There is no way they could find that much gold in\n"
"Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们不可能在\n"
"哥斯达黎加找到那么多黄金。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 7983..9153
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/8
msgid ""
"Columbus originally set sail in search of the\n"
"legendary land of gold.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥伦布最初出海是为了寻找\n"
"传说中的黄金之地。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 9320..9961
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/9
msgid ""
"Maybe he was just nuts about the stuff.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许他就是痴迷那玩意儿。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 9975..10644
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/10
msgid ""
"Costa Rica is rich enough without it.\n"
msgstr ""
"没黄金也够富饶。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 10727..11800
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/11
msgid ""
"Look at the forests and the animals, and the\n"
"peace-loving people...\n"
msgstr ""
"看看森林、动物，还有\n"
"热爱和平的人民……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 11814..12329
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/12
msgid ""
"That is what I want to protect.\n"
msgstr ""
"那才是我要保护的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 12357..12914
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/13
msgid ""
"...I know how you feel.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我懂你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 473..1825
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/0
msgid ""
"Democracy took root in Costa Rica before\n"
"anywhere else in Central America.\n"
msgstr ""
"民主在哥斯达黎加扎根，\n"
"比中美洲任何地方都早。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 1894..3162
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/1
msgid ""
"Sure, we had coups and dictators and all, but\n"
"never a total meltdown.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们也有过政变和独裁，但\n"
"从未彻底崩溃。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 3287..4026
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/2
msgid ""
"That is, until 26 years ago...\n"
msgstr ""
"直到26年前……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 4082..5726
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/3
msgid ""
"The civil war. Yeah, I understand you lost your\n"
"grandparents.\n"
msgstr ""
"内战。是啊，我明白你失去了你的\n"
"祖父母。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 5753..6868
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/4
msgid ""
"It started with a dispute over alleged fraud in the\n"
"presidential election.\n"
msgstr ""
"起因是对总统选举中涉嫌舞弊的\n"
"争议。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 6993..8108
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/5
msgid ""
"What I don't understand is why friend turned\n"
"against friend\n"
msgstr ""
"我不明白的是，为什么朋友会\n"
"反目成仇\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 8192..8735
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/6
msgid ""
"when they could have talked it out instead.\n"
msgstr ""
"明明本可以谈开的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 8832..9613
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/7
msgid ""
"Yeah, that... would have been nice.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，那样……就好了。\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/8
msgid ""
"Even today, some buildings still have bullet holes\n"
"from the civil war.\n"
msgstr ""
"即使在今天，一些建筑上仍留有内战时期的\n"
"弹孔。\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/9
msgid ""
"A quarter century later, and it is a tragedy we\n"
"ticos cannot forget... Must not forget.\n"
msgstr ""
"二十五年过去，这是我们哥斯达黎加人\n"
"不能忘……绝不该忘的悲剧。\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/10
msgid ""
"It was the year after the civil war that the army\n"
"was constitutionally abolished.\n"
msgstr ""
"内战结束后的那一年，军队\n"
"被依宪法废除。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/0
msgid ""
"A new president was elected this year - President\n"
"Oduber.\n"
msgstr ""
"今年选出了新总统——\n"
"奥杜贝尔总统。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/1
msgid ""
"He seems to be distancing himself from the United\n"
"States.\n"
msgstr ""
"他似乎正在与美国\n"
"保持距离。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/2
msgid ""
"He's limited the privileges granted to American\n"
"banks, lifted the sanctions on Cuba...\n"
msgstr ""
"他限制了给予美国银行的\n"
"特权，解除了对古巴的制裁……\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/3
msgid ""
"Our last president was so pro-U.S., people\n"
"suspected he was in bed with the CIA.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们的上一任总统极其亲美，人们\n"
"怀疑他与中情局有染。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/4
msgid ""
"You think the CIA's doing this because it feels\n"
"threatened by the president's shift in policy...?\n"
msgstr ""
"你认为中情局这么做是因为它感到\n"
"受到总统政策转变的威胁……？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/5
msgid ""
"It is possible. But would they really bring in such a\n"
"huge army just because of that?\n"
msgstr ""
"有可能。但他们会仅仅因为这一点就出动\n"
"如此庞大的军队吗？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/6
msgid ""
"Part of our job is finding out.\n"
msgstr ""
"查明真相也是我们的工作之一。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/7
msgid ""
"Exactly. Thanks, Snake. Peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。谢了，SNAKE。和平。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 487..1755
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/0
msgid ""
"So are you a student at the University for Peace,\n"
"Paz?\n"
msgstr ""
"那么，你是和平大学的学生吗，\n"
"帕兹？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 1797..2410
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/1
msgid ""
"No, I am still in high school.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，我还在上高中。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 2479..3761
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/2
msgid ""
"But Professor Gálvez lets me visit his office and\n"
"study with him every now and then.\n"
msgstr ""
"但加尔维斯教授允许我时不时去他的办公室\n"
"和他一起学习。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 3817..5419
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/3
msgid ""
"International law, security, conflict resolution,\n"
"human rights...\n"
msgstr ""
"国际法、安全、冲突解决、\n"
"人权……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 5489..6729
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/4
msgid ""
"We study all these subjects and then use them to\n"
"build the foundations of peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们学习所有这些科目，然后用它们来\n"
"构建和平的基础。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 6798..8373
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/5
msgid ""
"Yeah, I get it... I'd just never heard the UN had a\n"
"University for Peace before.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，我明白……我只是从没听说联合国有一所\n"
"和平大学。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 8387..10685
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/6
msgid ""
"Oh, that. Well, to be precise, it is still being set up.\n"
"They have started conducting research, but\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，那个。准确说，它还在筹建中。\n"
"他们已开始研究，但\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 10741..11563
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/7
msgid ""
"the UN has not passed the necessary resolution\n"
"yet.\n"
msgstr ""
"联合国尚未通过必要的\n"
"决议。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 11633..12260
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/8
msgid ""
"Professor Gálvez couldn't wait that long...\n"
msgstr ""
"加尔维斯教授等不了那么久……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 12274..12928
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/9
msgid ""
"Oh, uh, right.\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，对。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 12942..13514
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/10
msgid ""
"Costa Rica abolished its army,\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加废除了军队，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 13555..14586
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/11
msgid ""
"and has also hosted the Central American Court of\n"
"Justice.\n"
msgstr ""
"还曾承办过中美洲\n"
"法院。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 14614..15993
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/12
msgid ""
"It is the perfect place to build a university like\n"
"ours, don't you think?\n"
msgstr ""
"在这里建我们这样的大学再合适不过，\n"
"你不觉得吗？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/0
msgid ""
"Professor Gálvez was a KGB spy...?\n"
msgstr ""
"加尔维斯教授是克格勃间谍……？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/1
msgid ""
"I thought he helped me out of genuine concern for\n"
"Costa Rica's future...\n"
msgstr ""
"我还以为他是真心为哥斯达黎加的未来\n"
"才帮我的……\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/2
msgid ""
"You didn't know?\n"
msgstr ""
"你不知道？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/3
msgid ""
"How could I?! Believe me, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"我怎么会知道？！相信我，SNAKE。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/4
msgid ""
"He introduced himself as a peace researcher at\n"
"the university.\n"
msgstr ""
"他自我介绍说是大学里的\n"
"和平研究员。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/5
msgid ""
"He had an office and credentials and everything...\n"
msgstr ""
"有办公室、证件，一应俱全……\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/6
msgid ""
"They're masters at creating cover personas. They\n"
"think of everything\n"
msgstr ""
"他们是伪造身份的高手。他们\n"
"考虑到了一切\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/7
msgid ""
"- ID papers, jobs, sometimes even families.\n"
msgstr ""
"ID、工作，有时连家人都有。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/8
msgid ""
"Don't feel bad you didn't see through it.\n"
msgstr ""
"没看穿也别自责。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/9
msgid ""
"But you did?\n"
msgstr ""
"那你看穿了？\n"
